From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:15:56 -0400
Subject: feat: a tab dragged onto the page makes a split, and five more of the
 backlog

The owner's choices of 2026-10-20 for six rows of the backlog, in one patch
because they share the command bar, the preferences, Settings' Stedding page
and the tab row (patches/README.md, the round-patch exception):

- A split by dropping a tab on the page (S-113, GitHub issue 7; splits J10
  to J15): from the sidebar, the rail or the horizontal strip, the half of
  the page under the pointer lights in the Space's colour and a drop makes a
  split there, with the dropped page active; no window tears off while the
  pointer is inside the window; essentials, Space pins, splits, groups and
  browser pages are refused.
- The tab shown after the one on screen closes (S-112; tabs R33 to R38): the
  Space's most recently used tab, then the row below, then the one above;
  essentials only when the Space has no tab of its own; the same choice for
  Sleep Tab and Cmd-W on a pin.
- At launch only the selected tab loads (S-110; tabs R45 to R48, settings
  T22): "On startup, load" the selected tab, the essentials too, or the whole
  active Space, the rest coming back asleep.
- Tabs sleep on a timer and under memory pressure (S-111; tabs R39 to R44,
  settings T21, commandbar K34): "Put tabs to sleep after" (Never by
  default) through the sleep gate; Chromium's discards respect the same
  gate, and a split sleeps whole; Sleep Other Tabs rows; Memory Saver's card
  hidden.
- Page pictures in the hover card on the Mac too (S-115; pins H19 to H23),
  held in memory only; a slept row and an open card now update at once.
- With the address row hidden, its controls in the command bar (S-104;
  toolbar T39, T40, commandbar K31 to K33, shortcuts Z9): a row per extension
  action, media controls and site information; Cmd-E (Ctrl+Alt+E) cycles the
  extensions; popups and page info open at the page card's corner.

Tests: each feature's new unit and browser tests, each failing with its
product change taken out (H20 asserts an upstream behaviour and has none).

Why: the owner's next items, and a user's request for drag-to-split.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next re-cut gives each feature a patch
of its own (patches/README.md).
