+// With the address row not drawn, what it held stays reachable from the
+// command bar's actions mode (docs/features/toolbar.md T13, T39, T40;
+// commandbar K31-K33; BACKLOG S-104): every extension action, the media
+// controls and the page's site information are rows, and Cmd-E (Ctrl+Alt+E
+// off the Mac) runs an extension. A popup asked for while the row is hidden
+// opens inside the window at the page card's top edge, and the row stays
+// hidden.
+//
+// The rows run through the bar's own keys and the chord through the window's
+// command; the chord's release is the bar's seam, since a test sends no key
+// to the system. A popup is a window of its own that must show, so the
+// browser window stays above the others, and the fixture runs in the serial
+// leg (tooling/dev, SERIAL_BROWSER_TESTS).
