+// A picture of the page in the hover card (docs/features/pins.md H19-H23,
+// BACKLOG S-115). Chromium's hover-card preview images are on, on the Mac
+// as on Windows: a row that is not on screen shows a picture of its page
+// as last seen above the title and the pin's line (H8). Nothing on screen
+// gets one. A sleeping row keeps its picture and is not woken by a hover.
+// The pictures are held in memory only: none comes back after a restart,
+// and none is written to the profile. Chrome's own Appearance switch turns
+// them off.
+//
+// The hover is the controller's own call, as Chromium's hover card tests
+// make it, so no real pointer moves. A picture is copied from what the page
+// painted, and a window covered by another paints nothing: the window stays
+// above the others, and the fixture runs in the serial leg (tooling/dev,
+// SERIAL_BROWSER_TESTS).
